    <p class="paraHeader">THE REVELATION NO ONE TALKS ABOUT</p>  
    <p class="paraCommon">  Internships are NOT about learning skills. They are about <b>unlearning the wrong idea of education.</b></p>  
    <p class="paraCommon">  For 200+ years, we have carried a silent hallucination: <b>that education happens in classrooms… and real work begins “afterwards.”</b></p>  
    <p class="paraCommon">  But the world flipped - work flipped - identity flipped. Only education refused to flip.</p>  
    <p class="paraCommon">  And here’s the truth no one says openly: <b> **“Internships are not an add-on to education.</b> They are the correction to a flawed education model.”**</p>  
    <p class="paraCommon">  This is the thin line missing in every academic, corporate, and policy conversation and the line we are putting front and center.</p>  

